# Vulnerability details

**Description:**

The `RankedBattle::claimNRN` function allows players to claim NRN rewards without first staking NRN, which violates the protocol invariant that gamers must stake NRN to win NRN rewards through Ranked Battles.

**Impact:**

The ability to claim NRN rewards without staking NRN undermines the economic model and fairness of the Protocol. It allows players to receive rewards without contributing to the staking pool, potentially leading to an imbalance in the distribution of rewards and undermining the incentive structure of the game

**Proof of Concept:**

The `RankedBattle::claimNRN` doesn't check whether a player has staked NRN before they are able to call claimNRN and mint NRN. You can see the function below :

```
function claimNRN() external {
    require(numRoundsClaimed[msg.sender] < roundId, "Already claimed NRNs for this period");
    uint256 claimableNRN = 0;
    uint256 nrnDistribution;
    uint32 lowerBound = numRoundsClaimed[msg.sender];
    for (uint32 currentRound = lowerBound; currentRound < roundId; currentRound++) {
        nrnDistribution = getNrnDistribution(currentRound);
        claimableNRN += (
            accumulatedPointsPerAddress[msg.sender][currentRound] * nrnDistribution
        ) / totalAccumulatedPoints[currentRound];
        numRoundsClaimed[msg.sender] += 1;
    }
    if (claimableNRN > 0) {
        amountClaimed[msg.sender] += claimableNRN;
        _neuronInstance.mint(msg.sender, claimableNRN);
        emit Claimed(msg.sender, claimableNRN);
    }
}
```

**Recommended Mitigation:**

To address this issue, you should add a check in the claimNRN function to ensure that the caller has staked NRN before they can claim NRN rewards. This can be done by checking the staked amount for the caller in the amountStaked mapping.
