# Vulnerability details

## Description

The project relies on an off-chain server to invoke `RankedBattle::updateBattleRecord()` after a battle is started off-chain. The function deducts the voltage balance from the user who is the owner of the token ID that initiated the battle. This is passed as the function input `initiatorBool` to the function, which is set to `true` if the token ID initiated the battle:

```solidity
if (initiatorBool) {
    _voltageManagerInstance.spendVoltage(fighterOwner, VOLTAGE_COST);
}
```

The function determines who the owner is of the token ID, and deducts the voltage from them.

An attacker can leverage this to grief another user of their voltages. The attacker can initiate several battles, and immediately transfer the NFT that was used to initiate the battle to the victim user. Now, when the server calls `RankedBattle::updateBattleRecord()`, the owner of the NFT will be determined to be the victim user, and they will be charged for the voltage for the battles which the attacker actually initiated.

The attacker can use this method to grief a target user of their voltages.

## Impact

This attack allows an attacker to drain the victim of their voltage - including any extra voltages that the victim user might have bought. 

## Proof of concept

Put the test in this file: `test/RankedBattle.t.sol`
Run using: `forge test --match-test "testTransferNFTToExhaustVoltage"`

