# Vulnerability details

The `RankedBattle` contract may be vulnerable to an exploit where a player, acting as an attacker, can intentionally revert the `updateBattleRecord()` transaction by setting their voltage to an amount less than the required threshold of 10. This allows the attacker to observe the result of the battle by monitoring the failed transaction before it is finalized on-chain. The attacker can then take actions to mitigate negative consequences, such as unstaking NRN tokens to avoid having their stake put at risk after a loss.

## Impact
This can lead to an unfair advantage for players who exploit this issue, as they can avoid penalties that other players would face. 

## Proof of Concept
The game server use the `updateBattleRecord()` function to update the result of a battle, and it is during this time that the initiator's voltage is spent. Therefore, before the `updateBattleRecord()` transaction is processed, a player may deliberately call `spendVoltage()` to reduce their voltage below the required threshold of 10 units. This intentional action is taken with the knowledge that it will cause the `updateBattleRecord()` transaction to revert due to the player having insufficient voltage.

