# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The user could avoid loss by depleting his voltage before every `updateBattleRecord` call that would result in a loss.
## Proof of Concept
A game server will publish the battle results on the chain by calling an `updateBattleRecord` and providing relevant values as parameters. The battle could either end in a win, tie, or loss. The win and tie are good for the battle initiator as he doesn't lose anything. 

In case of a loss, user will lose points if he has any or he will lose a part of a stake. If the user is the initiator of the battle, then he can prevent a loss from happening by `depleting his voltage` with a frontrun call.

```solidity
function updateBattleRecord(
    uint256 tokenId,
    uint256 mergingPortion,
    uint8 battleResult,
    uint256 eloFactor,
    bool initiatorBool
)
    external
{
   ...
    _updateRecord(tokenId, battleResult);
    ...
    if (initiatorBool) {
        _voltageManagerInstance.spendVoltage(fighterOwner, VOLTAGE_COST);   <- WANTS TO SPEND VOLTAGE
    }

    totalBattles += 1;
}
```

A user could frontrun this call with a `spendVoltage` call and replenish (if possible) and drain the voltage below the amount needed for the execution of the above call.

```solidity
function spendVoltage(address spender, uint8 voltageSpent) public {
    require(spender == msg.sender || allowedVoltageSpenders[msg.sender]);
    if (ownerVoltageReplenishTime[spender] <= block.timestamp) {
        _replenishVoltage(spender);
    }

    ownerVoltage[spender] -= voltageSpent;
    emit VoltageRemaining(spender, ownerVoltage[spender]);
}
```

