# Vulnerability details

## Vulnerability details
When a player loses a PvP battle, the `_gameServerAddress` calls the `RankedBattles::updateBattleRecord` function to update the player's record. If the [player has accumulated points in the current `round`, those points are reduced](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-ai-arena/blob/main/src/RankedBattle.sol#L479-L490). Otherwise, a portion of their staked tokens is transferred to the [`StakeAtRisk` contract, putting the tokens at potential risk of loss](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-ai-arena/blob/main/src/RankedBattle.sol#L493-L497).

However, players can circumvent these consequences by front-running the `updateBattleRecord` transaction from `_gameServerAddress`.  This is possible due to the implementation of `spendVoltage` function:

    function spendVoltage(address spender, uint8 voltageSpent) public {
        //@audit-info if spender is msg.sender, then allow spending
        require(spender == msg.sender || allowedVoltageSpenders[msg.sender]);
        if (ownerVoltageReplenishTime[spender] <= block.timestamp) {
            _replenishVoltage(spender);
        }
        //@audit-info reduce voltage by voltageSpent
        ownerVoltage[spender] -= voltageSpent;
        emit VoltageRemaining(spender, ownerVoltage[spender]);
    }

This function allows a player to [manually deplete their own Voltage](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-ai-arena/blob/main/src/VoltageManager.sol#L106). Since `updateBattleRecord` [requires fighters to have sufficient Voltage for PvP result submission](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-ai-arena/blob/main/src/RankedBattle.sol#L334-L338) (only if initiator is fighter), a malicious player can intentionally expend Voltage to prevent a loss from being recorded.

