# Vulnerability details

## Description 
The constructor of the `aiArenaHelper` contract contains two separate initializations for the attribute probabilities of generation 0. The first is through the `addAttributeProbabilities` function, and the second is via a for loop that directly sets the `attributeProbabilities` mapping. This redundancy not only results in unnecessary gas consumption during contract deployment but also violates the protocol's design principle of single initialization, potentially leading to logical errors.
```solidity
    /// @dev Constructor to initialize the contract with the attribute probabilities for gen 0.
    /// @param probabilities An array of attribute probabilities for the generation.
    constructor(uint8[][] memory probabilities) {
        _ownerAddress = msg.sender;

        // Initialize the probabilities for each attribute
        addAttributeProbabilities(0, probabilities);

        uint256 attributesLength = attributes.length;
        for (uint8 i = 0; i < attributesLength; i++) {
            attributeProbabilities[0][attributes[i]] = probabilities[i];
            attributeToDnaDivisor[attributes[i]] = defaultAttributeDivisor[i];
        }
    } 
```
The impact of this issue is high because this violates the protocol's design principles. The double initialization could lead to confusion among developers and maintainers, and it may cause logical errors if future modifications are made with the assumption that initialization occurs only once.

