# Vulnerability details

## Description
Staking factor is used to calculate the amount of points you win (or lose) in a fight. These points then count to your chances of winning a merged fighter or part of the `NRN` awarded each round.

Staking factor is calculated based on your stake and stake at risk in [`RankedBattle::_getStakingFactor`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-ai-arena/blob/main/src/RankedBattle.sol#L526-L534):
```solidity
File: src/RankedBattle.sol

526:    {
527:      uint256 stakingFactor_ = FixedPointMathLib.sqrt(
528:          (amountStaked[tokenId] + stakeAtRisk) / 10**18
529:      );
          // @audit user with very little stake will still get rewards here
530:      if (stakingFactor_ == 0) {
531:        stakingFactor_ = 1;
532:      }
533:      return stakingFactor_;
534:    }    
```

The issue here is that the `stakingFactor` is normalized to the amount of tokens then rounded _in favor_ of the player.

Hence a player can stake dust, `1 wei` `NRN` and still get `1` as staking factor.

This `1 wei` of staked NRN isn't even at risk when losing as it will be rounded down to `0` when `stakeAtRisk` is calculated (as long as `bpsLostPerLoss != 10_000`):
[`RankedBattle::_addResultPoints`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-02-ai-arena/blob/main/src/RankedBattle.sol#L439):
```solidity
File: src/RankedBattle.sol

439:        curStakeAtRisk = (bpsLostPerLoss * (amountStaked[tokenId] + stakeAtRisk)) / 10**4;
```

## Impact
A user can stake dust and still get an, albeit small, portion of rewards.

