# Vulnerability details

`VoltageManager#spendVoltage` allows users to spend their voltage (L106):
```solidity
File: VoltageManager.sol
105:     function spendVoltage(address spender, uint8 voltageSpent) public {
106:         require(spender == msg.sender || allowedVoltageSpenders[msg.sender]);
107:         if (ownerVoltageReplenishTime[spender] <= block.timestamp) {
108:             _replenishVoltage(spender);
109:         }
110:         ownerVoltage[spender] -= voltageSpent;
111:         emit VoltageRemaining(spender, ownerVoltage[spender]);
112:     }
```

At the same time voltage is needed for the successful execution of the `updateBattleRecord` function in case a user is an initiator of the battle.
So calling `spendVoltage` would make it possible to DOS the `updateBattleRecord` function in case the user doesn't like the battle result.

## Impact
Users can spend their voltage to front-run and DOS `updateBattleRecord` function and prevent updating their results in case the battle is lost. 

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider removing the possibility for users to spend their voltage bypassing allowed spenders.


