# Vulnerability details

## Description
In AI arena fighters engage in battles with other fighters during rounds. Battle results are updated by the game server after every battle through `RankedBattle.updateBattleRecord`.  Fighter owners stake NRN on their fighters in `RankedBattle.stakeNRN` in order to gain or lose points when they win or lose battles. Also, battle losers would get part of their staked NRN depleted if they have no point to lose for that round. An internal function `RankedBattle._addResultPoints` calculates points to add or deduct and also staked NRN to collect from the loser and send to the `stakeAtRisk` contract. 
```
File:src/RankedBattle.sol
function updateBattleRecord(
        uint256 tokenId, 
        uint256 mergingPortion,
        uint8 battleResult,
        uint256 eloFactor,
        bool initiatorBool
    ) 
        external 
    {  
     ...........
      _updateRecord(tokenId, battleResult);
        uint256 stakeAtRisk = _stakeAtRiskInstance.getStakeAtRisk(tokenId);
        if (amountStaked[tokenId] + stakeAtRisk > 0) {
            _addResultPoints(battleResult, tokenId, eloFactor, mergingPortion, fighterOwner);
        }
      ...............
}
```
The error comes from the way the `curStakeAtRisk` is calculated in the internal function `_addResultPoints`. The staked NRN to be deducted from the user's stake is calculated as 
- curStakeAtRisk = (bpsLostPerLoss * (amountStaked[tokenId] + stakeAtRisk)) / 10**4;

There is an assumption that staked NRN  would always return 18 decimals which is not so. Therefore, users can stake certain amounts of token that would round down to 0. With a bpsLostPerLoss set to 10, 9.99*10**2 tokens would return 0. Therefore, the curStakeAtRisk would return 0.

