# Vulnerability details

## Impact
A user could exploit the system by staking a small amount of tokens effectively gaining points without putting staked NRN at risk.

When a user loses a battle part of his staked funds go to stakeAtRisk.
In order to gain points first he has to recover the stake at risk funds by winning battles, but this is not the case when the stake is less than a certain amount - more specifically `10 000 / bpsLostPerLoss` , which in the current implementation is equal to `1000` . The reason behind this is the way `curStakeAtRisk` is calculated - If the staked amount is less than `1000` it rounds down to 0, not putting stake at risk. The malicious user gains an advantage because he does not have to recover `fundsAtRisk` before gaining points.

