# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There is a vulnerability present in `claimRewards` function in `MergingPool` contract, that will permanently DOS users (having more than 2 unclaimed NFT) from claiming NFTs.

This happens because the `claimRewards` function specifies the size of the array argument `customAttributes[]` to be of size 2. So when a user having more than 2 unclaimed NFT( for example 3 NFTs) calls the function, then after minting each NFT, the function increases the `claimIndex` variable by 1. So after minting 2 NFTs, the value of `claimIndex` becomes 2, and in #L158, it tries to fill the index position 2 of the `customAttributes` array. But the array has only index `0` and `1`, because of the defined size. Thus this results in an "array out-of-bounds access" error.

So the users having more than 2 unclaimed NFT will never be able to claim their rewards. The `claimRewards` function will permanently be DOSed for them.

