# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The protocol allows users to re-roll their fighters, the re-roll function accepts a token ID as a parameter. However, it accepts the token ID as a `uint8`, it has the following signature `reRoll(uint8 tokenId, uint8 fighterType)`, and fighter IDs are of type `uint256`, so any fighter who has an ID > 255 (which is the max of uint8) can never be re-rolled as it can't fit in `uint8` and the transaction will revert.

## Proof of Concept

```
function testBugCantRerollFighter() public {
    address player;

    for (uint256 i; i < 257; i++) {
        address tmpPlayer = vm.addr(i + 1);
        _mintFromMergingPool(tmpPlayer);

        if (i == 256) player = tmpPlayer;
    }

    _fundUserWith4kNeuronByTreasury(player);

    uint256 fighterId = 256;

    assertEq(_fighterFarmContract.ownerOf(fighterId), player);

    vm.prank(player);
    vm.expectRevert(); // 256 is > uint8 limit (255)
    _fighterFarmContract.reRoll(uint8(fighterId), 0);
}
```

## Tools Used

Manual review + vs code

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Use `uint256` instead of `uint8` in the `reRoll` function parameter.











