# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The `updateBattleRecord` function, executed by the game server, updates battle records. It includes a check to ensure that the initiator has sufficient voltage, reverting the transaction otherwise. 

An initiator could spend all their voltage via `_voltageManagerContract.spendVoltage` prior to the commencement of a game, resulting in all transaction attempts being reverted. Consequently, a fighter can repeatedly prompt the game server to execute `_rankedBattleContract.updateBattleRecord()`, effectively enabling them to bypass loss record updates. 

This vulnerability is of high severity as it allows an initiator fighter to selectively update records for wins while avoiding losses, thereby manipulating their win-loss record.

